							Final Canvassing of Voter List 








	

		
			Pursuant to Rhode Island election law, the Board of Canvassers conducts a Final Canvass of Voters prior to each election. During the canvass, the voter registration list is reviewed and updated to ensure the accuracy of the Town's voter records and to process any pending voter registration matters.FINAL CANVASSING OF BRISTOL VOTER LISTThe Bristol Board of Canvassers will meet at Bristol Town Hall, 10 Court Street, on Tuesday, October 13, 2026, at 2:00 p.m. The meeting is for the purpose of canvassing the Preliminary List of Bristol Voters, and to hear objections to the inclusion or omission of any person as a registered voter, and to make a Final Canvass and correction of the voter registration file for the General Election that is to take place on Tuesday, November 3, 2026. The Preliminary List of Bristol Voters will be posted on Friday, October 9, 2026, in the Canvassing Department Office, Bristol Town Hall, 10 Court St, Bristol, RI; an updated list will be reposted on Wednesday, October 14, 2026. Posted: September 28, 2026Advertised:  October 1 and October 8Residents are encouraged to verify their voter registration status prior to the applicable voter registration deadline. Additional election information and important dates may be found on the Town's Elections page.
		
	



